WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Two real Flutter clients in one local match, initially connected through different Java workers.

00:03.000 --> 00:04.500
One Java worker is abruptly stopped. Redis and the other worker remain available.

00:04.500 --> 00:09.300
Client B reconnects to the same match. Selected player-visible state is preserved; Client A's socket stayed open.

00:09.300 --> 00:11.600
Client B's WebSocket is explicitly closed to exercise automatic reconnection again.

00:11.600 --> 00:17.720
The client recovers the same match and selected state again. Both local recovery scenarios passed.
